@div version 1 (Old Babylonian version)

1.1. saŋ-ki gid₂-da {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: saŋki[forehead]; gid[long]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: After @wDN{Enlil's} frown had slain @wSN{Kiš} as  
#etcsl: line-id=1.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 18; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 12; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 17

1.2. kiš{ki} gud an-na-gin₇ im-ug₅-ga-ta
#lem: Kiš[1]SN; gud[bull]; an[sky]; ug[kill]
#tr.en: if it were the Bull of Heaven, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.2

